", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CVMc4A5cHPR6EiuAYTpJiq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions after it was deployed (us-east, us-west, eu-west; error rate 18%). We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the service on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second attempt finished in all regions. checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 everywhere and healthy, with a 0.2% error rate. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging but still went to production), and investigate the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0174fuTMoxLbCtp55vssbu94", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001. checkout-api is healthy again.\n\n- **Rollback:** I went back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 had been failing health checks in all three regions, with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback problem:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on different versions. The second attempt finished in all three. Now us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate and on-call was paged only once. The incident says what happened and what was done, and lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, also failed health checks in staging but still went to production.\n  - Investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}